      "sparse_rank": null,
      "text": "`r Biocpkg(\"SingleR\")` is an automatic annotation method for single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNAseq) data [@aran2019reference].\nGiven a reference dataset of samples (single-cell or bulk) with known labels, \nit labels new cells from a test dataset based on similarity to the reference.",
      "title": "pinned_singler_vignette",
      "tool_name": "singler",
      "tool_names": []
    },
    {
      "canonical_task": "",
      "chunk_id": "approved-v2:bf28f60dbfacce443e310e6f",
      "claim_type": "method",
      "dense_rank": null,
      "governance_status": "approved_scientific_assertion",
      "recommendation_eligible": false,
      "score": 14.0,
      "source_bound": true,
      "source_id": "source-revision:d426b082f012b8be5a4f74cf",
      "source_span": "source-artifact:fae57c993608662cdadcfe96e8543864/text-sha256:c26f06dddfe2259c8668798a3d52fa7c3b528cd07c3d6ead82f85e89d971d0e9:58538:59475",
      "sparse_rank": null,
      "text": "Cell type annotation of single cells (SingleR). The SingleR pipeline is based on \ncorrelating gene expression of pure cell types with single-cell gene expression. \nSingleR can be used with any reference data set. For mouse samples, we used the \nImmGen database, a collection of 830 microarray samples, which we classified to \n20 main cell types and further annotated to 253 subtypes12; a data set of 358 mouse \nRNA-seq samples annotated to 28 cell types collected, processed, and shared, \ncourtesy of Bérénice Benayoun, can also be used. For human samples we used \nthe data sets from Blueprint Epigenomics, 144 RNA-seq pure immune samples \nannotated to 28 cell types14, and Encode, 115 RNA-seq pure stroma and immune \nsamples annotated to 17 cell types13. More reference data sets for mouse and \nhuman are available with the SingleR R package. For specific applications, smaller \ndata sets can be applicable (as demonstrated in Fig. 2c).",
      "title": "paper_SingleR_CAND_PUB_SingleR_2019_Aran",
      "tool_name": "singler",
      "tool_names": []
    },
    {
      "canonical_task": "",
      "chunk_id": "approved-v2:da656b7a304bf427841ba866",
      "claim_type": "method",
      "dense_rank": null,
      "governance_status": "approved_scientific_assertion",
      "recommendation_eligible": false,
      "score": 14.0,
      "source_bound": true,
      "source_id": "source-revision:aac7d6351f74cbc7c4ab775d",
      "source_span": "source-artifact:5c01eb692907d03c08112688ef39f065/text-sha256:7184174fa7d638ad433c0145c0c850a1ce80347093bc05517e669caebadebc8b:387:594",
      "sparse_rank": null,
      "text": "Performs unbiased cell type recognition from single-cell RNA sequencing data, by leveraging reference transcriptomic datasets of pure cell types to infer the cell of origin of each single cell independently.",
      "title": "recovered_c744746dfe8e1d26",
      "tool_name": "singler",
      "tool_names": []
    }
